@startuml uc-plan-changes
!include _theme.iuml

state planChanges as "planChanges()" {

  state " " as RequestingPlan
  state " " as Observing
  state " " as Classifying
  state " " as Presenting

  [*] --> RequestingPlan
  note on link
  <b>Operator</b> asks what would change, for an explicit
  policy and a deliberately narrow selection
  end note

  RequestingPlan --> Observing
  note on link
  <b>Octoform</b> resolves policy, discovers the selection and
  reads only the state the policy is about
  end note

  Observing --> Classifying
  note on link
  <b>Octoform</b> sorts every candidate into one category
  • change: observed and desired values differ
  • no change: they already agree
  • warning: available, with a known consequence
  • blocked: availability or state cannot be proven
  end note

  Classifying --> Presenting
  note on link
  <b>Octoform</b> presents the plan and changes nothing
  • blocked work stays in the report and is never
    handed to the applier
  • accounts run one at a time, so reports do not
    interleave
  end note

  Presenting --> [*]
  note on link
  <b>Operator</b> confirms scope, current values, desired
  values, warnings and blocked work before acting
  end note
}

planChanges --> PLAN_PRESENTED
note on link
executable changes were found; exit 1
end note

planChanges -[#A78BFA]-> PLAN_PRESENTED
note on link
nothing to do, exit 0 · something blocked,
exit 4 · the run itself failed, exit 5
end note
@enduml
